From 14900323a193b0aca1c3849a2331933dac96d6d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Ciocaltea <cristian.ciocaltea@collabora.com>
Date: Wed, 6 Aug 2025 18:11:02 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] gitlab-ci: Use a newer archlinux-kernel-builder image

Building the Arch package for kernel v6.15 (via pacman-pkg make target)
revealed an unexpected increase in size since v6.11, i.e. from
136 MB to 231 MB, which means ~70%.

The initial assumption was that it might be related to some of the
config changes introduced by upstream Arch package.  This proved to be
wrong soon after started the investigation, since building the same
v6.15 tree with the configurations previously used for v6.11 did not
result in a size reduction.

Extending the build tests on a few mainline kernels revealed the problem
only affects v6.15, since any of the older releases verified (e.g.
v6.14) did not exhibit the behavior.

Surprisingly, after switching to a local build environment, the package
size for v6.15 kernel went back to normal.  The only obvious difference
in the setup stemmed from the GCC version: 14.2.1 (on the CI side) vs.
15.1.1 (locally).

Updating the kernel builder image in the linux-integration CI
environment had the effect of switching to GCC 15.1.1 and, implicitly,
fixed the size issue.

Make use of the newer archlinux-kernel-builder Docker image.

Signed-off-by: Cristian Ciocaltea <cristian.ciocaltea@collabora.com>
Signed-off-by: Henry Paradiz <henry.paradiz@gmail.com>
---
 .gitlab-ci.yml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.gitlab-ci.yml b/.gitlab-ci.yml
index c4aebd4b61ed..2ef9d7352b7e 100644
--- a/.gitlab-ci.yml
+++ b/.gitlab-ci.yml
@@ -98,7 +98,7 @@ build-debian-kernel-builder:
     IMAGE_DISTRO_BASE: archlinux
     IMAGE_DISTRO_TAG: base-devel
     IMAGE_NAME: archlinux-kernel-builder
-    IMAGE_TAG: "2024-12-02"
+    IMAGE_TAG: "2025-08-02"
 
 check-archlinux-kernel-builder:
   extends:
-- 
